# MAQAM production deploy notes
# What the current server needed, so a move to a new one repeats it. No secrets here: keys live in the server's .env only.

## 1. Server (current: Hostinger shared hosting)
- SSH: ssh -p 65002 u780982159@92.113.18.14   (hPanel: https://hpanel.hostinger.com/)
- App folder:  ~/domains/maqam-eg.com/maqam        (Laravel project)
- Web root:    ~/domains/maqam-eg.com/public_html  (serves the app's public/)
- The project needs PHP >= 8.4. The server's default `php` (/usr/bin/php) is 8.2 and fails with
  "Composer detected issues in your platform". Use PHP 8.5 at /opt/alt/php85/usr/bin/php.
  For the SSH shell, once per server:

echo 'alias php=/opt/alt/php85/usr/bin/php' >> ~/.bashrc
echo 'alias composer="/opt/alt/php85/usr/bin/php /usr/local/bin/composer"' >> ~/.bashrc
source ~/.bashrc

## 2. Every deploy
cd ~/domains/maqam-eg.com/maqam
# pull / upload the new code, then:
composer install --no-dev --optimize-autoloader
php artisan migrate --force
php artisan optimize:clear

## 3. Cron job (required: push notifications and location geocoding run from the scheduler)
- hPanel > Cron Jobs > type **Custom** (NOT "PHP": that type forces the 8.2 binary and prefixes
  /home/u780982159/ to whatever you type). Every minute (* * * * *):

/opt/alt/php85/usr/bin/php /home/u780982159/domains/maqam-eg.com/maqam/artisan schedule:run

- Without it, pushes wait in the queue forever and customers' phones get nothing.
  Admin > Notifications shows when pushes are stuck.

## 4. .env essentials
APP_ENV=production
APP_DEBUG=false
APP_URL=https://maqam-eg.com          # https; Kashier callback/webhook URLs are built from it
QUEUE_CONNECTION=database

### Kashier (payments) — keys from the Kashier dashboard in **Live** mode
KASHIER_MODE=live
KASHIER_MID=MID-xxxxx-xxx             # must be set: config falls back to a test MID
KASHIER_PAYMENT_API_KEY=...
KASHIER_SECRET_KEY=...                # also verifies the webhook signature
KASHIER_CURRENCY=EGP
KASHIER_SSL_VERIFY=true
# optional, built from APP_URL when empty:
# KASHIER_MERCHANT_REDIRECT=https://maqam-eg.com/payment/kashier/callback
# KASHIER_SERVER_WEBHOOK=https://maqam-eg.com/payment/kashier/webhook

Kashier dashboard > Webhooks:
- URL: https://maqam-eg.com/payment/kashier/webhook
- Custom headers: none (Kashier signs with x-kashier-signature by itself)
- Events: Transaction - Success, Transaction - Failed (nothing else is handled)
- "Test Webhook" answering 400 Invalid signature / 404 Order not found = reachable and working.

### Senderbot (WhatsApp: sign-in codes and order messages)
SENDER_BOT_URL=https://sender.reachrapid.net
SENDER_BOT=...                        # bearer token
SENDER_BOT_SESSION=maqam
- Pair the WhatsApp number from Admin > WhatsApp (scan the QR).
- The session can drop on Senderbot's side by itself. Symptom in storage/logs/laravel.log:
  "Senderbot: send message failed ... Session not found" → re-pair from Admin > WhatsApp.
- The session name actually in use is stored in Admin > Settings > whatsapp > senderbot_session_id.

### Firebase (push)
- Service account JSON at storage/app/private/firebase/service-account.json (or FIREBASE_CREDENTIALS=path)
- FIREBASE_WEB_* keys for browser notifications on the website.

### Other
GEMINI_API_KEY=...                    # chatbot / performance summaries

After editing .env: php artisan config:clear (and config:cache again if you cache config).

## 5. Store settings (Admin > Settings > store)
- shipping_cost (default 35.00) and free_shipping_threshold (default 500.00) come from a migration;
  edit them there.

## 5b. Nothing depends on a seeder
- Every setting the code reads is created by a migration (`migrate --force` is enough on a fresh server);
  edit the values in Admin > Settings.
- Ranks, prize types, products etc. are created from the dashboard.
- Mobile app wording: Admin > App texts. Only changed texts are stored (table app_texts); the app keeps
  its own text for the rest. resources/app_texts/defaults.json lists the app's texts — refresh it with
  `php artisan app-texts:sync` after the app's strings change (needs the "mobile app" folder next to it).

